README-NEWS -- three news systems, and which one to takeIf you are setting up Usenet news on your own OS-9 system you want ONE newssystem.  This file is here so you do not have to install all three to findout how they differ.Short answer: take MNews with nn if you want to read news in comfort.  Itbrings a full-screen newsreader, nn, it needs no Microware module, and allof it is built from the source on this disk.  Take UUCPbb'snews if you already run UUCPbb for mail and want the small set that livesbeside it.  C News's six tools are helpers from a larger system; they arenot a news system you can run by themselves.THE THREE---------                   UUCPbb 2.1 news     C News              MNews + nn  ------------------------------------------------------------------------  directory        CMDS/UUCP           CMDS/NEWS           CMDS/MNEWS  programs         6                   6                   11, and `setup'  bytes            116146              63012               410646  needs cio        yes, all six        yes, all six        no  files articles   rnews               --                  inews (rnews                                                           hands on to it)  reader           readnews: prompts   --                  nn: full screen  posts            postnews            --                  inews, nnaux  spool            SPOOL/news          --                  SPOOL/MNEWS  article names    COMP/OS/OS9/a1      --                  comp/os/os9/1  active file      SYS/UUCP/active     --                  USR/LIB/NEWS/Active  source           SRC/uucpbb          SRC/cnews           SRC/mnews  docs             DOC/uucpbb          DOC/cnews           DOC/mnews, DOC/nn  UUCPbb   rnews 22348, readnews 33162, postnews 26526, expire 15472,           subscribe 9308, unsubscribe 9330.  Bob Billson's, GPL v2.  C News   bdecode 8818, byteflip 1882, c7decode 2304, dbz 13344,           newshist 31908, newslock 4756.  Geoff Collyer 